WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.810
<v Examiner>Huntington's disease.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.543
<v Examiner>Five marks.

3
00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:09.454
<v Examiner>Explain Huntington's disease as a genetic disease: its cause, how it damages the body,

4
00:00:09.454 --> 00:00:15.168
<v Examiner>how it's inherited, and the chance of an affected child when one parent is big H little h,

5
00:00:15.168 --> 00:00:17.391
<v Examiner>and the other is little h little h.

6
00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:22.797
It's on her help board for Module 3, and it comes back in the final, in case 15.

7
00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:24.966
So learn it once, and use it twice.

8
00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:30.734
The hook: chromosome four, a stutter in the gene, a toxic protein in the brain.

9
00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.349
And one big H is enough.

10
00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.492
The cause.

11
00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:37.648
Huntington's is caused by a mutated gene on chromosome four,

12
00:00:37.648 --> 00:00:40.072
and chromosome four is an autosome.

13
00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:44.851
Her help board puts it in numbers: humans have forty-six chromosomes,

14
00:00:44.851 --> 00:00:47.967
forty-four autosomes and two sex chromosomes.

15
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:49.845
What the mutation is.

16
00:00:49.845 --> 00:00:55.214
A copying error during DNA replication, for example while sperm are being made.

17
00:00:55.214 --> 00:00:58.680
The base sequence C A G is repeated too many times:

18
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:04.321
thirty-six to a hundred and twenty times, instead of the normal ten to thirty-five.

19
00:01:04.321 --> 00:01:06.700
Think of it as the gene stuttering.

20
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.751
How it damages the body.

21
00:01:08.751 --> 00:01:13.219
The longer gene makes a larger, abnormal protein called huntingtin.

22
00:01:13.219 --> 00:01:13.953
It's toxic.

23
00:01:13.953 --> 00:01:19.555
It builds up in the brain and damages brain cells, especially the ones for movement,

24
00:01:19.555 --> 00:01:20.889
thinking and memory.

25
00:01:22.339 --> 00:01:23.617
How it's inherited.

26
00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:24.896
Autosomal dominant.

27
00:01:24.896 --> 00:01:30.211
One copy of the mutated allele, big H little h, is enough to cause the disease,

28
00:01:30.211 --> 00:01:32.566
and it can come from either parent.

29
00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:35.325
That means there are no healthy carriers.

30
00:01:35.325 --> 00:01:40.910
Anyone with a big H develops the disease, and only little h little h is unaffected.

31
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.861
It shows in every generation.

32
00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:44.008
The cross.

33
00:01:44.008 --> 00:01:47.281
Big H little h, crossed with little h little h.

34
00:01:47.281 --> 00:01:51.459
Two boxes are big H little h, and two are little h little h.

35
00:01:51.459 --> 00:01:55.429
Each child has a fifty per cent chance of being affected.

36
00:01:56.879 --> 00:01:57.562
The traps.

37
00:01:57.562 --> 00:02:01.454
Dominant means big H little h is affected, not a carrier.

38
00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:05.894
Her deck asks it straight out: can a person be a healthy carrier?

39
00:02:05.894 --> 00:02:06.099
No.

40
00:02:06.099 --> 00:02:10.265
Second: chromosome four is an autosome, not a sex chromosome.

41
00:02:10.265 --> 00:02:15.319
Third: it's a gene mutation, a repeat, not an extra or missing chromosome,

42
00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:16.889
so it isn't aneuploidy.

43
00:02:17.339 --> 00:02:17.893
<v Examiner>Once more.

44
00:02:17.893 --> 00:02:21.713
<v Examiner>Huntington's: the cause, the damage, the inheritance, and the chance.

45
00:02:24.163 --> 00:02:27.035
A mutated gene on chromosome four, an autosome:

46
00:02:27.035 --> 00:02:32.351
C A G repeated thirty-six to a hundred and twenty times, instead of ten to thirty-five.

47
00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:37.606
It makes an abnormal, toxic huntingtin protein that builds up in the brain and damages

48
00:02:37.606 --> 00:02:39.440
movement, thinking and memory.

49
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:44.023
It's autosomal dominant: one copy is enough, there are no healthy carriers,

50
00:02:44.023 --> 00:02:46.039
and it shows in every generation.

51
00:02:46.039 --> 00:02:48.911
Big H little h, crossed with little h little h,

52
00:02:48.911 --> 00:02:51.661
gives a fifty per cent chance for each child.
